WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:11.039
[Gentle music]
Blazor components get the same C# engine as the rest of your code. Hover any expression in the markup, and Roslyn answers, with your XML docs.

00:16.817 --> 00:25.904
Completion works inside Razor expressions too. The members come from Roslyn, and each edit lands in the Razor file, never in generated code.

00:38.250 --> 00:47.168
The markup around it is still HTML. Element names and HTML hovers come from VS Code's own HTML service.

01:01.417 --> 01:07.765
Make a mistake, and the error shows on the Razor line that caused it, in the editor and in the Problems panel.

01:25.983 --> 01:35.729
Go to Definition jumps from the markup into the code block. Find All References lists every use in the Razor file, with the generated scaffolding left out.

01:44.217 --> 01:48.335
Rename a field in the code block, and every use in the markup follows.

02:01.083 --> 02:07.536
From C#, Go to Definition on a component opens its Razor file, not a generated class.

02:20.050 --> 02:25.848
Rename a tag, and its closing tag changes with it. Elements and code blocks fold, too.
